     1  *        *>--- conformance-case
     2  *        *> id: pb5987-declaratives-after-paragraph
     3  *        *> rules: [FMT-14.2.1]
     4  *        *> source-format: free
     5  *        *> portable: unverified
     6  *        *>---
     7  *              *> kb/Work PB5987. A DECLARATIVES portion written after a paragraph of a d
        +        ivision without sections is out of
     8  *              *> place by the same rule (§1985:IV.6.4.1.1, §2023:14.3): COBOL2797.
     9                  IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
    10                  PROGRAM-ID. PB5987AP.
    11                  ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
    12                  INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
    13                  FILE-CONTROL.
    14                      SELECT F ASSIGN TO "PB5987AP.TMP".
    15                  DATA DIVISION.
    16                  FILE SECTION.
    17                  FD F.
    18                  01 F-REC PIC X(4).
    19                  PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    20                  MAIN-P.
                        ^
                 ==> error COBOL2797 (col 8): PROCEDURE DIVISION: paragraph MAIN-P is not in a section — the procedure division has
                     DECLARATIVES, which only §1985:IV.6.4.1.4.2 Format 1 (with-sections) admits, and §1985:IV.6.4.1.2: "If one
                     paragraph is in a section, all paragraphs must be in sections".
    21                      DISPLAY "B".
    22                      STOP RUN.
    23                  DECLARATIVES.
                        ^
                 ==> error COBOL2797 (col 8): PROCEDURE DIVISION: a DECLARATIVES portion that follows a nondeclarative section,
                     paragraph or sentence — §1985:IV.6.4.1.1: "Declarative sections must be grouped at the beginning of the
                     Procedure Division", so §1985:IV.6.4.1.4.2 Format 1 prints the DECLARATIVES … END DECLARATIVES portion
                     immediately after the procedure division header.
    24                  ERR-S SECTION.
    25                      USE AFTER STANDARD ERROR PROCEDURE ON F.
    26                  ERR-P.
    27                      DISPLAY "IN-DECLARATIVES".
    28                  END DECLARATIVES.
    29
